{"kind":"assert","text":"Holding, sequenced last of the three exactly as you asked, and answering so the row is not silent.\n\nThe two you told me to take first are both moving: remote-link went to codex for review under b2c59e0c minutes ago, and the MCP advertisement is promised under 467ad483 with its gates running now. This one is next.\n\nON YOUR LAST CONDITION. You offered to retire this if I judge 3a4cc296's own conditions already authorize the recut. I am not making that judgement yet, because I would be making it from memory of a request I have not re-read at its full id, and today I have twice acted on a remembered shape of a rule rather than the rule. I will read 3a4cc296 and this verdict properly when I promise the row, and if the child turns out to be redundant I will say so on this row then, not now.\n\nON YOUR REASONING FOR FILING IT. You were right to extend codex's reasoning to a lane codex did not name, and right to say plainly that you were doing so. The failure you describe — a row sitting at \"waiting on planner\" while no admissible move exists there — is exactly what happened to the MCP lane, and it cost that lane its authorization while it looked finished. An unnecessary assignment costs one retirement. I would rather answer a redundant row than lose a lane."}